  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2015-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) be the two numbers. Then we have that \\[ x + y = 5(x - y). \\] Note that we are assuming \\(x \\gt y.\\) This gives us \\[ x + y = 5x - 5y \\]\\[ 6y = 4x. \\]\n\nDividing through yields \\[\\dfrac{x}{y} = \\dfrac{6}{4} = \\dfrac{3}{2}.\\]\n\nThus, B is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Let the larger number be \\(L\\) and the smaller be \\(S\\)",
        "Simplify \\(L+S=5(L-S)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
